<section image-layout="blank" id="0xg5rYGE5Z" vertical-align="end" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.38" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/WMImjznaq1xA7ohbNfI94.png" saved-media-id="aa1xcfn81d0o28e" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="practical-light-afterimage" alt="High-contrast editorial studio photograph of anonymous hands holding a sheet of black paper at the far right while a narrow bone-white beam enters through a cut aperture and leaves a controlled coral and amber afterimage across the frame, left third kept as deep near-black negative space, practical hard light, restrained film grain, no faces, logos, text, or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="-o8t41BcbA" vertical-align="end"><display size="lg">Make room<br>for the <span text-color="accent">unexpected</span></display><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="lg" style="padding-right: 45%;">Experimentation is how surprise becomes evidence.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="BXIZ3SSShi" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="qls7Vu29yQ"><display size="md" font-size="50pt">A perfect plan can only deliver<br><span text-color="accent">what it already knows</span></display><spacer size="18pt"></spacer><grid divider="sm neutral-border"><grid-item id="AuoJBBTJN4" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Efficiency</p><p font-size="lg">Standardized execution reduces variation when the destination is known. Applied too early, it can erase the evidence discovery needs.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="PBMVRhi4A1" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">The creative paradox</p><p font-size="lg">We need enough structure to act, with enough openness to encounter something we did not prescribe.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="_Np8jQTVbx"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="m8DqskFA_p"><p role="eyebrow">Operating modes</p><h2>Two loops. Two outcomes.</h2><p>Match the loop to what is known.</p><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="_80yDR2fOI" background-color="surface" padding="10pt 18pt" rowspan="24"><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="HZMEzy_ZFf" colspan="14"><p role="eyebrow">Production loop</p><h3>Known target</h3><p role="caption">Repeat protects fidelity.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="TX630WeWOQ" colspan="46"><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="chevron" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-fill="true" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="1em" style="--marker-chip-padding: 0.75em;"><grid-item id="FyQ9r03SmP" colspan="15"><h4>Define</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="1J3j5Kaq_N" colspan="15"><h4>Execute</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="r9xDs13weO" colspan="15"><h4>Verify</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="3_kooOjzu6" colspan="15"><h4>Repeat</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="MfmlklHZc0" background-color="surface" cell-decor="side-line" padding="10pt 18pt" rowspan="24"><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="Ww8Rd_EfkT" colspan="14"><p role="eyebrow">Discovery loop</p><h3><span text-color="accent">Open question</span></h3><p role="caption">Learning changes the frame.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="aluszlnQ3J" colspan="46"><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="chevron" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-fill="true" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="1em" style="--marker-chip-padding: 0.75em;"><grid-item id="Tk58RZVMNd" colspan="12"><h4>Frame</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="bLr9GUChm5" colspan="12"><h4>Vary</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="aWxTqS-T0V" colspan="12"><h4>Notice</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="Um5WVKVy7O" colspan="12"><h4>Select</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="ecyeQbahqP" colspan="12"><h4>Learn</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="iYA9ydr-sW" background-color="accent" padding="8pt 18pt" rowspan="12"><h4>Known destination: reduce variation. Unknown destination: create informative variation.</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="TCTK_0ycka"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="lny8p3dvzs"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative worked example</p><h2>Not a brainstorm. A bounded bet.</h2><p font-size="lg">The question sets the boundary; the boundary makes the evidence interpretable.</p><spacer size="14pt"></spacer><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="cwekr6Po4x" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="17"><p role="eyebrow">1 · Question</p><h3>Can a six-word brief produce usable surprise?</h3><p role="caption">Name what the experiment must teach.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="sLQfcEmDc2" vertical-align="center" colspan="4"><p font-size="32pt" align="center"><span text-color="accent">→</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="yrxTHSLz0R" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="18"><p role="eyebrow">2 · Test boundary</p><h4>Constants</h4><p>Monochrome · 30 minutes</p><hr color="neutral-border"><h4>Variable</h4><p>One changed rule per round</p></grid-item><grid-item id="qX--WgZ2zl" vertical-align="center" colspan="4"><p font-size="32pt" align="center"><span text-color="accent">→</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="XNSW_t6cDE" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="17"><p role="eyebrow">3 · Decision gate</p><h4>Signal</h4><p>Surprising and usable from at least two of three reviewers.</p><hr color="neutral-border"><h4>Stop</h4><p>After four rounds and 24 departures.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer size="16pt"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="94mG05NZa6" background-color="accent" padding="14pt 18pt"><h4>A bounded bet changes one variable while the question, evidence, and decision stay visible.</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="85QdNt_8Zc"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Z4-icj9ppD" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.46" vertical-align="end" colspan="37"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/zlXaxNT7FC_JUZ80qhToy.png" saved-media-id="1hmqybjrh03uj9m" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="practical-light-afterimage" alt="High-contrast overhead editorial studio photograph of anonymous hands interrupting a straight path of black paper with a small glass prism, one hard coral beam diverted into an amber trace with a faint ultraviolet residual afterimage, practical hard light, deep negative space around ordinary cutting and drawing tools, restrained grain, no faces, logos, text, or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><p role="eyebrow">Deliberate variation</p><h1>Design the interruption</h1><p font-size="lg">Change one thing strongly enough to create evidence, not noise.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="RsrW0Ojr2d" background-color="surface" padding="38pt 32pt" colspan="23"><p role="eyebrow">Change one axis</p><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="Bwta66beku" cell-style="subtle"><h3>Material</h3><p>Translate the idea into another medium.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Lr9WebJ4Ca" cell-style="subtle"><h3>Rule</h3><p>Remove a familiar option or impose an unlikely limit.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="-oEuA8XkA9" cell-style="subtle"><h3>Perspective</h3><p>Let another discipline, audience, or scale reshape the question.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="sm">One interruption at a time keeps the lesson visible.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="YSFiJ61EK-" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="dt4rVXayuh"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative exercise—not measured conference data</p><h2>One brief, 24 departures</h2><p>Generate broadly first. Apply the evidence gate second.</p><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="cdfq_SwvPY" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Generation field · 4 rounds × 6 each</p><table col-widths="[22,13,13,13,13,13,13]" header-row="true" borders="all" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Round</p></td><td><p>A</p></td><td><p>B</p></td><td><p>C</p></td><td><p>D</p></td><td><p>E</p></td><td><p>F</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td><td><p><span text-color="accent">●</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p role="caption">Each dot is one departure; one rule changes per round. No observed advance count is claimed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="gR0LHengDi" vertical-align="center" colspan="4"><p font-size="32pt" align="center"><span text-color="accent">→</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="LckDnOLEJ5" background-color="surface" padding="18pt" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="solid">Review gate</label></labels><display size="md">3</display><p>independent reviewers</p><p role="eyebrow">Two marks</p><h4>Surprising + usable</h4><hr color="neutral-border"><display size="md">2 of 3</display><p>must give both marks for an idea to advance.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="iTgqq3PFHC"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="o_XANNhydt"><h2>Open a 72-hour aperture</h2><p font-size="lg">Act before the idea becomes precious.</p><smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>Today</h4><p>Write one question and name the constants.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Tomorrow</h4><p>Run three variations with one changed rule.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Within 72 hours</h4><p>Show two people, record their signals, and choose what continues.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><spacer size="16pt"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="PUz2ridco3" background-color="accent" padding="14pt 18pt"><h4>What did the interruption reveal that the plan concealed?</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="2c8VJsD1TL" vertical-align="end" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.42" card-margin-hidden="true"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/y51aL5DS_jH1dld2ID2jD.png" saved-media-id="qoj0v6qbppcfehj" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="practical-light-afterimage" alt="High-contrast editorial studio photograph of a near-black doorway standing slightly open on the right, a narrow bone-white rectangle of practical hard light crossing the floor, one amber long-exposure line passing through the opening and leaving a faint ultraviolet residual trace, deep uncluttered negative space on the left, restrained film grain, no people, logos, text, or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="7SmFbo4AlK" vertical-align="end" colspan="31"><p role="eyebrow">Protect the promise. Loosen the route.</p><display size="lg">Leave a door<br><span text-color="accent">open</span></display><p font-size="lg">Name the promise. Fix one constraint. Change one variable. Keep only what earns its place.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><h3 role="subheading">Rigor does not eliminate the unexpected. It creates a way to recognize it.</h3></grid-item><spacer span="29"></spacer></grid></section>